			"widgets_values":[
				"Please accurately identify and extract all sounds present in the target video. Present them **as single independent words only** (no phrases, sentences, or explanatory text). Organize them by sound type to ensure no omissions or redundancies.\n\n## Core Requirements\n1. Sound words must accurately match the actual audio in the video; no fictional sounds are allowed.\n2. Only output the words themselves, each standing independently, with similar sounds grouped together.\n3. Cover all recognizable sounds (including faint background noises and short transition sounds).\n\nSound Word Examples & Scene-Specific Supplements\n\n1. Natural Environment Sounds\n- Wind, Rain, Thunder, Birdsong, Cicada, Stream, Wave, Leaf-rustle, Snow, Frog, Insect, Waterfall, Pine-sigh, Hail, Mist, Dew-drop\n\n2. Urban Life Sounds\n- Car-horn, Brake, Engine, Honk, Footstep, Door-close, Elevator, Keyboard, Phone-ring, Knock, Street-hum, Subway-announcement, Bus-announcement, Crowd-murmur, Vendor-call, AC-hum, Fridge-hum, Microwave-beep\n\n3. Action & Interaction Sounds\n- Door-open, Typing, Page-turn, Paper-tear, Paper-cut, Tap, Collision, Rub, Tear, Squeeze, Unlock, Water-pour, Stir, Chop, Sizzle, Dish-wash, Mop, Sweep, Hammer, Zipper, Button-rub\n\n4. Human-Related Sounds\n- Speech, Laugh, Cry, Cough, Sneeze, Breath, Whisper, Shout, Cheer, Sigh, Burp, Swallow, Clap, Stamp, Whistle, Hum\n\n5. Mechanical & Electronic Sounds\n- Alarm, Phone-vibrate, Current, Printer, Scanner, Hairdryer, Vacuum, Washing-machine, TV-on, Computer-boot, Camera-shutter, Recorder-button, Doorbell, Siren, Oven-beep\n\n6. Special Scene Sounds\n- Fire-crackle, Firework, Firecracker, Glass-shatter, Metal-clink, Water-spray, Bubble-pop, Gear-turn, Rope-rub, Horse-hoof, Wheel-roll, Plane-takeoff, Train-horn, Ship-whistle, Gunshot, Explosion, Piano, Guitar, Drum, Violin\n\nFood Making \n- Slice, Dice, Chop, Stir-fry, Fry, Simmer, Steam, Bake, Blend, Grind, Juice, Strain, Brew, Boil, Bubble, Crisp, Crunch, Chew, Bag-tear, Can-open, Oil-pour, Powder-sprinkle, Meat-chop, Peel, Pit, Dough-knead, Roll, Ferment, Roast, Oven-out, Cool, Plate\n\nOutdoor Adventure \n- Hiking-stick-tap, Gravel-rub, Branch-snap, Breath, Wind, Birdsong, Stream, Waterfall, Leaf-fall, Snow-crunch, Ice-crack, Campfire-crackle, Tent-zipper, Backpack-rub, Water-bottle-pour, Map-flip, Compass-spin, Mosquito-hum, Animal-howl, Thunder, Rain, Hail, Mist-drop, Grass-step, Rock-step, Mud-step, Rope-rub, Climb-tap\n\nWorkplace Office \n- Typing, Mouse-click, Keyboard-tap, Page-turn, Paper-tear, Staple, Bind, Print, Scan, Copy, Phone-ring, Call, Whisper, Cough, Footstep, Door-open, Door-close, Elevator-run, AC-hum, Water-dispenser, Coffee-brew, Pen-write, Eraser, File-stack, Drawer-open, Drawer-close, Meeting-vote, Applause, Projector-on, Mic-static\n\nHome Daily Life\n- Wake-up, Dress, Groom, Brush-teeth, Wash-face, Comb-hair, Hairdryer, Shaver, Water-flow, Toilet-flush, Cook, Dish-wash, Mop, Sweep, Vacuum, Table-wipe, Clothes-organize, Fold, Zipper, Button, Door-open, Door-close, TV-on, Remote-click, Phone-vibrate, Alarm, Microwave-beep, Fridge-hum, Washing-machine-run, Hang-clothes, Collect-clothes, Scissor-cut, Tape-stick\n\nSports & Fitness \n- Run, Jump-rope, Step, Dumbbell-clink, Barbell-drop, Equipment-rub, Breath, Heartbeat, Sweat-drop, Yoga-mat-rub, Stretch, Squat, Push-up, Sit-up, Ball-bounce, Ball-hit, Pass, Whistle, Crowd-cheer, Sneaker-rub, Towel-wipe, Bottle-open, Drink, Pant, Shout, Count\n\nMaternal & Child \n- Cry, Coo, Gurgle, Suck, Burp, Sneeze, Giggle, Babble, Lullaby, Rattle, Crib-creak, Bottle-suck, Diaper-rub, Pacifier-suck, Rock, Whisper, Kiss, Pat, Swing, Blanket-rustle\n\nPets \n- Bark, Meow, Purr, Hiss, Growl, Whine, Howl, Scratch, Paw-tap, Tail-wag, Bowl-clink, Treat-crunch, Leash-jingle, Cage-open, Lick, Sniff, Sneeze, Yelp, Chew, Scramble\n\nTravel \n- Plane-takeoff, Plane-land, Luggage-roll, Door-card-beep, Hotel-door-open, Train-whistle, Bus-hum, Ferry-horn, Airport-announcement, Ticket-tear, Map-flip, Camera-shutter, Umbrella-open, Sand-crunch, Wave-crash, Temple-bell, Market-holler, Bike-bell, Backpack-zip, Water-bottle-pour\n\nGaming \n- Button-click, Joystick-move, Explosion, Gunshot, Sword-clink, Spell-cast, Level-up, Coin-collect, Enemy-groan, Character-voice, Footstep, Jump, Dash, Hit, Shield-clang, Potion-pour, Chest-open, Trap-trigger, Rain, Wind, Fire-crackle\n\nCampus \n- Bell, Lecture, Book-flip, Chalk-write, Eraser-wipe, Pen-click, Notebook-turn, Whisper, Laugh, Hallway-footstep, Library-hush, Class-begin, Class-end, Backpack-zip, Lunch-box-open, Food-crunch, Sports-whistle, Team-cheer, Lab-equipment, Marker-write\n\nWedding \n- Ring-clink, Applause, Vow, Choir, Piano, Flower-toss, Dress-rustle, Shoe-click, Door-open, Kiss, Toast-clink, Confetti-crackle, Camera-shutter, Whisper, Cry, Laugh, Ribbon-tear, Invitation-flip, Chair-scrape, Music\n\nConcert\nCello, Flute, Trumpet, Harp, Clarinet, Oboe, Trombone, Organ, Bow-rub, String-pluck, Piano-key-tap, Drum-hit, Trumpet-blast, Mic-crackle, Speaker-hum, Curtain-rustle, Stage-creak, Instrument-tune, Bravo, Applause, Cheer, Whistle, Silence, Murmur",
